<description>
Complete every colored sprite by applying the union of all aligned partial sprite masks.

Input structure:
- The dominant color is the background.
- Each non-background color appears as a separated partial copy of one common sprite mask.
- The copies share a top-left-aligned sprite window; some copies may be missing lower or right edge pixels.

Rule:
- Crop each same-color mask to its bounding box.
- Pad the crops to the maximum observed height and width, aligned at the top-left, and OR them into one complete template.
- Fill that template at every sprite location using the sprite's own color.

Key insight:
- No single input sprite is complete, but their missing cells are complementary, so the aligned union reveals the full mask.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "same-color partial sprite masks, one per foreground color, sharing a top-left-aligned window",
  "transform": "pad smaller masks down/right to the largest observed window, recover the complete sprite as the union of all aligned masks, then fill that mask in each sprite window using that window's color"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 11-22 rows x 18-22 cols
  background: single dominant color
  template:
    shape: square, 5-7 cells per side
    fill_fraction: 0.48-0.84 of bounding box
    symmetry: LR + UD + rot90 + rot180 [observed]
    connectivity: 4-connected or 8-connected (1-4 components in 4-conn)
  sprites:
    count: 2-4 distinct foreground colors, each showing a partial copy of the same template
    placement: top-left aligned within a template-sized window; windows never overlap and have gap >= 1 cell
    damage: each sprite is missing 7-33% of template pixels (1-6 pixels), scattered randomly within the template mask
    coverage: union of ALL sprite masks exactly recovers the full template (every template pixel is present in >= 1 sprite)
  output:
    same grid; every sprite window is filled with the complete template in that sprite's color
    pixels only added, never removed or moved

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size (H x W) and background color
    2. Design the complete template as a square boolean mask (side 5-7); ensure fill 48-84%
    3. Choose N=2-4 foreground colors
    4. Place N non-overlapping template-sized windows on the grid with gap >= 1 cell between any pair; each window must fit within grid bounds
    5. For each sprite, randomly remove 7-33% of template ON-pixels to create a damaged copy; ensure the union of all damaged copies still covers every template pixel (repair any uncovered pixel by restoring it in a random sprite that had it removed)
    6. Write damaged sprites into input grid at their window positions; output grid gets full template at each window
```
</generation_spec>
